Q: HTML: set onclick event handler in external script file before user clicks it? A: <p>Things are loaded in the order that they have in the HTML document. Either you put the script element in the head element, so that it loads first, and then all the rest of the document is loaded after, making the <code>$(document).ready()</code> function nessary:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;html&gt;

&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;
    $(document).ready(function() {
      $("#submitA").on("click", function(event) {
        something();
      });
    });
    function something(){
      console.log('something');
    }
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;input value="Click here" type="submit" name="submitA" id="submitA" /&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;

&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>Or you load the script element in the end, where you know that all orther elements has been loaded:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;html&gt;

&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;input value="Click here" type="submit" name="submitA" id="submitA" /&gt;

  &lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;
    $("#submitA").on("click", function(event) {
      something();
    });
    function something(){
      console.log('something');
    }
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;

&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Filter a flat associative array using another flat associative array with PHP A: <p>It seems you want to compute the array_difference, you should use <a href="http://php.net/manual/en/function.array-diff.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">array_diff</a></p>

<pre><code>&lt;?php
$a1=array ( "291" =&gt; 3, "292" =&gt; 1, "293" =&gt; 3 );
$a2=array ( "291" =&gt; 3, "292" =&gt; 1 ) ;

$result=array_diff_assoc($a1,$a2);
print_r($result);
?&gt;
</code></pre>
